---
// What a Carton boundary holds, as compartments of one box: each is
// separate, and the dashed walls between them are the boundaries.
---

<section class="compartments not-content" aria-labelledby="holds">
  <h2 id="holds">What the boundary holds</h2>
  <div class="box">
    <article>
      <h3>Only exports cross</h3>
      <p>Other Cartons reach what a Carton exports and nothing else. Ruby's own <code>private_constant</code> hides the rest, across Boxes.</p>
      <pre><code><span class="c">Billing</span>::<span class="c">Invoice</span> <span class="r"># public</span>
<span class="c">Billing</span>::<span class="c">Tax</span>     <span class="x"># NameError</span></code></pre>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Monkey patches stay put</h3>
      <p>A patch to a builtin class, such as <code>String#blank?</code>, applies only inside the Carton that makes it.</p>
      <pre><code><span class="r"># in the cms Carton</span>
<span class="s">''</span>.blank?  <span class="r"># =&gt; true</span>
<span class="r"># everywhere else</span>
<span class="s">''</span>.blank?  <span class="x"># NoMethodError</span></code></pre>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Gem versions per Carton</h3>
      <p>Each Carton can set up its own bundle, so two Cartons can load different versions of the same gem in one process.</p>
      <pre><code><span class="r"># reports/Gemfile.lock</span>
bigdecimal (<span class="s">3.3.1</span>)
<span class="r"># pricing/Gemfile.lock</span>
bigdecimal (<span class="s">4.1.1</span>)</code></pre>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .compartments {
    padding-block: 2rem 1rem;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-h2);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    font-family: var(--carton-display);
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }

  .box {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    border: 2px dashed var(--carton-boundary);
    border-radius: 1rem;
    background: var(--carton-boundary-soft);
  }

  @media (min-width: 56rem) {
    .box {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  article {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  article + article {
    border-top: 2px dashed var(--carton-boundary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 56rem) {
    article + article {
      border-top: 0;
      border-left: 2px dashed var(--carton-boundary);
    }
  }

  h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }

  p {
    margin: 0.6rem 0 1.25rem;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  p code {
    font-size: 0.875em;
    padding: 0.05em 0.3em;
    border-radius: 0.25rem;
    background: var(--sl-color-bg-inline-code);
  }

  pre {
    margin: auto 0 0;
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    border-radius: 0.6rem;
    background: var(--carton-panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--carton-panel-edge);
    font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-1);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  pre code {
    background: none;
    padding: 0;
    font-size: inherit;
  }

  .c { color: var(--sl-color-white); font-weight: 650; }
  .s { color: #e8b04b; }
  .r { color: var(--sl-color-gray-3); }
  .x { color: var(--carton-error); }

  :root[data-theme='light'] .s { color: #9a5b00; }
</style>
